-- title:
--   Idempotents in compact semigroups of nonexpansive maps
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. Let the weak carrier of $K$ be compact Hausdorff.
--
--   1. **Convex families.** A family of weak selfmaps is convex if its image in the ambient function space is convex.
--   2. **Closure properties.** For a convex family $B$ of nonexpansive maps, members of its pointwise weak closure are approximated in norm at finitely many points by members of $B$. They are again nonexpansive, and the closure is closed under composition if $B$ is.
--   3. **Idempotent.** For a decreasing sequence $B_n$ of nonempty convex composition-closed families of nonexpansive maps, there is $P$ with
--   $$
--   P\in\bigcap_n\overline{B_n},\qquad P\circ P=P,\qquad P\text{ nonexpansive}.
--   $$
--   This follows from the Ellis–Numakura lemma for compact right-topological semigroups.
